  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat shows $11.3B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with 302 awards and an average award size of $37.4M. Obligations are down 47.2% year over year. Engineering Services is the largest market for Electric Boat at $6.9B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $4.4B. Fiscal-year obligations peaked at $21.4B in FY25 and are $11.3B in FY26 to date. Electric Boat also records smaller program dollars in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M, and in several manufacturing categories that range from $2.4M to $268K. The current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. The dataset separates award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables as total contract values, while the other figures are contract obligations. Readers looking at performance, market mix, or award sizing will find a heavy concentration in Engineering Services and Ship Building and Repairing, and a much smaller share across several specialized manufacturing NAICS codes.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Electric Boat's FY2026 obligations by market?",
        "body": "Engineering Services accounts for $6.9B of Electric Boat obligations in FY2026 to date. Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $4.4B. The remaining markets are much smaller, with the next-largest listed at $3.4M and other manufacturing NAICS entries ranging from $2.4M to $268K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY25 obligations were $21.4B while FY26 obligations are $11.3B to date. FY21 through FY24 show figures of $8.7B, $9.4B, $10.8B, and $8.6B respectively. Overall obligations are down 47.2% year over year."
      }
    ]
  },
